From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:52:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 485/488] [DS4.1] Greedy verification selects its targets from
 the gathered pairs, in one launch

Greedy verification launched select_first_argmax over the all-gathered shard
pairs, then the rejection kernel over its ids; at the launch floor the
selection stayed 1-9% behind Triton's. greedy_rejection_kernel now takes the
pairs: lane j of a request loads position start + j's pairs (every rank's,
before the first combine), reduces them in rank order with the selection's
combine (a total order, the masked pad pair included where the selection has
one), and stages the target and the draft it verifies in shared memory; lane 0
then runs the unchanged acceptance loop from there. The kernel is keyed by
(width, drafts dtype, ranks, pair width).

vocab_parallel_argmax becomes vocab_parallel_pairs (the gathered 16-byte pair
rows), greedy_rejection_sample takes them, the runner's two sites pass them,
and the greedy verification declares the fused kernel for its TP size instead
of the separate selection. The plain selection stays: DSpark's drafter
launches it for its last step and without a Markov table.

benchmark_tilelang_sampling.py's greedy_rejection case times the fused launch
against Triton's selection and verification.
